# GRIDE - the sources of GRIDEd, GRIDE 2.0, GRIDE 1.0 and the toolchain and Help they share. This working
# copy (D:\GRA\My Documents\GRIDEx3) builds; the repository it pushes to (GIT Test\GRIDE) only keeps.
# Build output is never committed. Git matches these without regard to case on Windows, so
# the toolchain's build\ folders are named by path: a plain `build/` would hide GRIDE 2.0's src\Build.
x64/
bin/
obj/
/toolchain/**/build/
.vs/
sandbox/
.gride/
examples/toolchain-demo/out/
*.user
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.obj
*.exe
*.lib
*.log
*.tlog
*.metagen
installer/dist/
# The third-party example's prebuilt library is a source of that example, not build output.
!/examples/projects/thirdparty-mathx/third_party/mathx/libs/**/*.lib
# The Mac's folder metadata and Python's byte-code caches are never committed.
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
